    ORT's own message blames PATH / LD_LIBRARY_PATH / GPU support, which is misleading: no amount
    of PATH fixing produces a `.so.10` or a `.so.12` that is not installed here.
    Nor is upgrading ORT the answer - `pip install -e .` pins this version, because
    `nvidia-modelopt[onnx]` requires `onnxruntime-gpu~=1.24.2`. Newer ORT wheels are still `cu12`
    and still TensorRT 10, so on this stack the GPU providers need a source build of ORT.
    This affects only ORT's *embedded* use of TensorRT; TensorRT itself, and every other example
    here, is unaffected - `case_reference_for_tensorrt` builds a real engine in this same process.

