    -> clearing one flag moved the disagreement by 312x.
       `BuilderFlag.TF32` is on by default, so a TensorRT engine built with no precision flags at
       all is *not* doing FP32 matmuls - it is doing TF32 ones on the tensor cores, with a 10-bit
       mantissa. Before blaming a conversion bug for a 1e-3 discrepancy, clear TF32 and re-measure:
       if the gap collapses, there is no bug, and the remaining ~1e-5 is ordinary reassociation.
